{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42581 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "Ferruginin B is consistently shown to target M-phase phosphoprotein 8, which is a known component of the cell cycle machinery. This protein is also a target of multiple structurally related compounds, including (2S,8S,8aR)-2-(3-hydroxyprop-1-en-2-yl)-8,8a-dimethyl-1,3,4,6,7,8-hexahydronaphthalen-2-ol and (6S)-6-[(2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxyoctadecanoic acid, all of which share a common mechanism of action. These compounds are all capable of binding to Histone H1.0, a critical histone that regulates chromatin structure and gene expression. The consistent targeting of M-phase phosphoprotein 8 by Ferruginin B and its related compounds suggests a shared biological pathway, potentially involving the regulation of the cell cycle and chromatin dynamics. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ferruginin B and Histone H1.0, though further investigation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction and its relevance to disease.",
